## Set multiple languages

If your audio spans a known set of languages rather than a single dominant one, Universal-3.5 Pro accepts the `language_codes` parameter (plural). Transcription is constrained to the languages you list while still code-switching among them:

```json theme={null}
{
  "audio_url": "https://assembly.ai/wildfires.mp3",
  "speech_models": ["universal-3-5-pro"],
  "language_codes": ["en", "es", "pt"]
}
```

A one-element list such as `["es"]` behaves exactly like setting `language_code` to `"es"`. `language_codes` is mutually exclusive with `language_code` and `language_detection`, so set only one of the three. For the full behavior, supported languages, and fallback rules, see [Code switching](/pre-recorded-audio/code-switching#constrain-the-language-set).

See the [Supported languages](/pre-recorded-audio/supported-languages) page for all supported languages and their codes.
